Package: libacvd4.0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: surface mesh coarsening and resampling on top of VTK - libraries
 ACVD (Approximated Centroidal Voronoi Diagrams) is a set of VTK-based
 libraries for fast isotropic and anisotropic mesh coarsening, remeshing and
 resampling, plus volume-processing helpers. It is the remeshing engine used
 by MITK's Remeshing module and by ShapeWorks.
 .
 This package contains the shared libraries (vtkSurface and
 vtkVolumeProcessing).

Package: libacvd-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends:
 libacvd4.0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 libvtk9-dev,
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: surface mesh coarsening and resampling on top of VTK - development
 ACVD (Approximated Centroidal Voronoi Diagrams) is a set of VTK-based
 libraries for fast isotropic and anisotropic mesh coarsening, remeshing and
 resampling, plus volume-processing helpers.
 .
 This package contains the headers (including the header-only
 DiscreteRemeshing templates) and the CMake configuration used via
 find_package(ACVD).
